src(9,'Jyotiraditya Scindia joins BJP','Indian Express','https://indianexpress.com/article/india/jyotiraditya-scindia-bjp-madhya-pradesh-6308812/','2020-03-11','Journalism','Joining, resignation and stated reasons','Joined BJP on 11 March after making his Congress resignation public on 10 March. Criticised Congress direction and Madhya Pradesh promises; praised Modi. BJP announced a Rajya Sabha nomination amid the exit of 22 Congress MLAs.','His explanation is attributed; private motives and unlawful inducements are not established.')
src(10,'Kamal Nath resigns ahead of trust vote','NDTV','https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/kamal-nath-resigns-as-madhya-pradesh-chief-minister-ahead-of-trust-vote-2197864','2020-03-20','Journalism','Resignation and competing reactions','Nath resigned before the planned floor test after 22 MLAs left. Nath criticised betrayal; Scindia said the government had departed from public welfare. Rebels said their decisions were voluntary, disputed by Congress.','Political allegations are competing claims, not findings of criminal wrongdoing.')
src(11,'Shivraj Singh Chouhan v Speaker, MP Legislative Assembly','Supreme Court; CaseMine reproduction','https://www.casemine.com/judgement/in/5e96d3253321bc784b911bcf','2020-04-13','Court judgment','Original judgment paras 43–57; operative order of 19 March reproduced at para57','Court upheld the call for a floor test and directed a 20 March sitting. Speaker’s resignation/disqualification powers were distinct. Members’ freedom to attend was protected; no compulsory meeting with Congress was ordered.','Original judicial text inspected, excluding website-generated summary. A confidence-test ruling does not establish personal criminal guilt or decide all political allegations.')
src(12,'MP polls: six Scindia loyalists lose, seven win','PTI / Rediff','https://www.rediff.com/news/report/mp-polls-6-scindia-loyalists-who-revolted-in-2020-lose-7-win/20231204.htm','2023-12-04','Journalism','Supporter cohort and Gwalior–Chambal results','Of a reported cohort of 19 close supporters who switched in 2020, six lacked 2023 tickets; seven of the 13 candidates won and six lost. BJP won 18 of 34 Gwalior–Chambal seats and Congress 16.','PTI defines the cohort. Party and supporter outcomes are not Scindia’s personal election results or a causal estimate of his influence.',origin='PTI-2023-12-04')
src(13,'Scindia supports integration of Jammu and Kashmir','NDTV','https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/article-370-jammu-and-kashmir-jyotiraditya-scindia-of-congress-backs-centre-on-jammu-and-kashmir-2081258','2019-08-06','Journalism','Quoted social-media statement','While in Congress, supported integration of Jammu and Kashmir and Ladakh but said constitutional process should have been followed.','A public position, not a parliamentary vote; preserve the procedural qualification.')
